<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Real life: hire purchase or a bank loan (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A {@item@} has a cash price of Ksh \( {@C0@} \). {@nm@} does not have the cash and is considering two options:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Hire purchase:</strong> a deposit of Ksh \( {@D0@} \) and \( {@n0@} \) monthly instalments of Ksh \( {@x0@} \).</li>
<li><strong>Bank loan:</strong> borrow the full cash price at \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum compound interest, and repay everything at the end of \( {@T0@} \) years.</li></ul>
<p>Give your answers to 2 decimal places where necessary.</p>
<p>(a) Total amount paid under hire purchase:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Total amount repaid on the bank loan:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Which option is cheaper?</p>
<div>[[input:ans3]]  [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(d) How much is saved by choosing the cheaper option?</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> \( H = {@D0@} + {@n0@} \times {@x0@} = {@H0@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \( {@C0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@R0@} }{100}\right)^{ {@T0@} } = {@r2(L0)@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> The {@cheapw@} is cheaper.</p>
<p><strong>(d)</strong> Saving \( = |{@H0@} - {@r2(L0)@}| = {@r2(abs(H0 - L0))@} \).</p>
<p>In real life, also consider things the numbers don't show: hire purchase lets you use the item while paying, while the bank loan needs a lump sum at the end.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
